:"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-1-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,530,1445,190]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-2","number":"1B","markdown":"Using Newton-Raphson method, find the real root of the equation\n\n$$\n\\cos x = 3x - 1\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is in radians, correct to three decimal places by taking $x_0 = 0.5$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-2-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,712,1445,180]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-3","number":"1C","markdown":"Using the following data, find $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $x = 0$.\n\n| $x$ | 0 | 0.1 | 0.2 | 0.3 | 0.4 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| $y$ | 1.0 | 0.9975 | 0.9900 | 0.9776 | 0.8604 |","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,884,1445,126],"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-3-diagram-1","caption":"Table of $x$ and $y$ values (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,884,1445,126]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-4","number":"2A","markdown":"Using Runge Kutta method of order 4, find $y(0.2)$, given\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^2-x^2}{y^2+x^2} \\quad \\text{with } y(0)=1\n$$\n\nwith $h = 0.2$. Correct to 4 decimal places.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1061,1445,149],"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-4-diagram-1","caption":"Differential equation $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{y^2-x^2}{y^2+x^2}$ with $y(0)=1$ (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1061,1445,149]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Using modified Euler's method, find\n\n$$\ny(1.4),\\ \\text{given that } \\frac{dy}{dx} = 1 + \\frac{y}{x} \\text{ with } y(1)=2 \\text{ by taking } h=0.2.\n$$\n\nCarry out 2 iterations in each step and correct to 4 decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1202,1445,167],"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-5-diagram-1","caption":"Differential equation $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=1+\\dfrac{y}{x}$ with $y(1)=2$ (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1202,1445,167]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Using Simpson's $\\dfrac{1}{3}$-rule, find an approximate value for the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_1^2 e^{-x/2}\\,dx.\n$$\n\nTake $h = 0.25$ and correct to 4 decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1361,1445,257],"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-6-diagram-1","caption":"Integral $\\int_1^2 e^{-x/2}\\,dx$ (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1361,1445,257]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process find an orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ from the set of vectors $\\{(1,1,2),(1,-1,2),(1,0,1)\\}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-8-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1610,1445,125]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Solve $(5x^4 + 3x^2y^2 - 2xy^3)\\,dx + (2x^3y - 3x^2y^2 - 5y^4)\\,dy = 0","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1,2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/773f8210eb9ed28ce5ab/q-9-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1726,1445,42]},{"src"